<article class="env-exercise" id="02EG">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02EG">Exercise <span data-tag="02EG">6.1.6.18</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a monoidal category containing objects $X$ and $Y$. Show that, if $X$ is weakly right dualizable and $Y$ is right dualizable, then the tensor product $X \otimes Y$ is weakly right dualizable (and that there is a canonical isomorphism $(X \otimes Y)^{\vee } \simeq Y^{\vee } \otimes X^{\vee }$). </p>
</article>
